1057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1031 "Units of Length" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1033 236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051057 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7da842dd-faa9-5816-a487-76ce9eea530c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186185700 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8b08e998-197e-5fff-8659-5d89e0f6dcbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188007 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188007 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a shoe box. What units could we use?\n\nI. $\\textrm{cm}^2$\n\nII. $\\textrm{cm}^3$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{kg}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cbff12b-cc20-5db4-9e64-8bb7b4c62dd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188007 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in centimeters $(\\textrm{cm}).$ When measuring lengths in centimeters, volumes are measured in $\\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm},$ which is usually written as $\\textrm{cm}^3.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188008 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188008 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7e/7e21a9afeb5a6c102a8426255b17112479144845be87f121435c8e27078610ab.png)\n\n What is the volume of the cube shown in the diagram above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188008 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "94639d5a-c922-52f3-8e50-82d0e9a3dbad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188008 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the volume $V$ of a cube, we cube its side length. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =(5\\,\\text{m})^{3} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{m}\\times 5\\,\\text{m}\\times 5\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =(5\\times 5\\times 5)\\times (\\text{m}\\times \\text{m}\\times \\text{m}) \\\\  & =125\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188009 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188009 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7e/7e300a90dbfda5a9210cec502c2879b7950e2765c433eb6ee6284e74db3cd220.png)\n\n What is the area of the square above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f153b4a-2706-5ff6-b0b3-65cfc29e1391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188009 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(5\\,\\text{ft})^{2} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{ft}\\times 5\\,\\text{ft} \\\\  & =(5\\times 5)\\times (\\text{ft}\\times \\text{ft}) \\\\  & =25\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Appropriate Units of Area and Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188300 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bec12e1c-bc47-5ac1-a1aa-f9de136b90cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing a Volume With the Correct Units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188301 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "469f0c76-3641-5a56-82bb-9ac807ff2017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing an Area With the Correct Units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188302 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "09b56d66-4e96-56de-b3fa-747cb2e3487d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1045 "Units of Area and Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186189124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188466 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "939b57fa-4d38-510c-b99b-f714aa08558b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186185700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a fish tank. What units could we use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "466efffd-5b60-5120-9dd7-a526b8962ba3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188570 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in inches $(\\text{in}).$ When measuring lengths in inches, volumes are measured in $\\text{in}\\times \\text{in}\\times \\text{in},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{in}}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189122 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189122 #edb/ref 1061 38276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189122 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4ce7e8a3-4577-50bf-a00f-068cd37af097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189122 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189123 #edb/ref 1061 38277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189123 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3fc81ced-9831-5655-a85b-a4d4b3264016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189123 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189124 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189124 #edb/ref 1061 38318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189124 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "81a881d6-35a5-534b-ad14-ce4e42142162" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189124 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189125 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189125 #edb/ref 1061 38328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189125 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f7ec5ae-5a69-500f-9fb4-8f461d1c2564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189125 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189130 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189130 #edb/ref 1061 38355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189130 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9c654269-ba54-5587-a9b6-ba5cb053ac2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189130 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189141 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189141 #edb/ref 1061 633751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189141 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d695cf8d-6531-5468-8016-c6cf9749344f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189141 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189242 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189242 #edb/ref 1061 45706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189242 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e659ead9-3e52-5de3-86a3-60522e000640" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189242 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189383 #edb/ref 1064 "**Area** measures how much space there is on a flat surface. In this lesson, we'll learn about the various measurement units of area and how they relate to units of length. \n\nConsider a square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{m},$ shown below. \n\n![](images/3f/3feaac95102a8a3014b7ab114adb97d5a0267a5c654c584bff03152801c807c2.png)\n\nTo find the area of a square, we multiply its side lengths. Therefore, the area of this square is equal to\n\n$$\n1\\,\\textrm{m}\\times 1\\,\\textrm{m} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}^2.\n$$\n\nThe unit of area $(\\textrm m^2)$ we used is called a **square meter.** In this case, we say that the area of our square is **one square meter.**\n\nIn previous lessons, we learned that length can also be measured in kilometers $(\\textrm{km}),$ centimeters $(\\textrm{cm}),$ and millimeters $(\\textrm{mm}).$ Each of these length units has a corresponding area unit:\n\n- A square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{km}$ has an area of $1\\,\\textrm{km}^2,$ or **one square kilometer**.\n\n- A square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{cm}$ has an area of $1\\,\\textrm{cm}^2,$ or **one square centimeter**.\n\n- A square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{mm}$ has an area of $1\\,\\textrm{mm}^2,$ or **one square millimeter**.\n\nThe same idea applies when measuring area in customary units. For example:\n\n- A square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{in}$ has an area of $1\\,\\textrm{in}^2,$ or **one square inch**.\n\n- A square with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{ft}$ has an area of $1\\,\\textrm{ft}^2,$ or **one square foot**." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189383 #edb/ref 1065 6332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189383 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "782bd823-d56b-501d-97cd-2346156da037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189383 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189385 #edb/ref 1064 "**Volume** measures how much three-dimensional space there is inside something. \n\nConsider a cube with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{m},$ shown below. \n\n![](images/f0/f0006ee19c09fcf56ad032675f5f71ca8e49fc4c554a169e17bff0a09f2bbb6a.png)\n\nTo find the volume of a cube, we multiply its side lengths. Therefore, the volume of this cube is equal to\n\n$$\n1\\,\\textrm{m}\\times 1\\,\\textrm{m}\\times 1\\,\\textrm{m} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}^3.\n$$\n\nThe unit of volume $(\\textrm m^3)$ we used is called a **cubic meter.** In this case, we say that the volume of our cube is **one cubic meter.**\n\nAs with area, each unit of length has a corresponding volume unit. For example:\n\n- A cube with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{cm}$ has a volume of $1\\,\\textrm{cm}^3,$ or **one cubic centimeter**.\n\n- A cube with sides of length $1\\,\\textrm{in}$ has a volume of $1\\,\\textrm{in}^3,$ or **one cubic inch**." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189385 #edb/ref 1065 6337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189385 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ad0f170d-4023-5465-9263-b8826bdaa467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189385 #edb/ref 1067 "Units of Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189389 #edb/ref 1064 "A square is a special type of rectangle whose length and width are equal. For example, consider the square below.\n\n![](images/a9/a92233299ba67fec2a7712c88afcabeff3973dda07afdd7f91c085c4564e2aa1.png)\n\nWe say that the **side length** of this square equals $3\\,\\textrm{m}.$\n\nSince a square is a special type of rectangle, we find its area by multiplying its length and width. However, since its length and width are equal, we can find its area by *squaring* its side length:\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(3\\,\\text{m})^{2}\\text{ } \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{m}\\times 3\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =(3\\times 3)\\times (\\text{m}\\times \\text{m}) \\\\  & =9\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189389 #edb/ref 1065 15346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189389 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4d7c3905-be55-58f4-8070-adad0bd8fef4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189389 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating Area" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189433 #edb/ref 1064 "A **cube** is a special type of rectangular solid whose length, width, and height are equal. \n\n![](images/e6/e696b4b9875052f18f394df4f0c6fb867b599a8484ac04acfca021ade9618a49.png)\n\nWe say that the **side length** of this cube equals $2\\,\\textrm{cm}.$\n\nSince a cube is a special type of rectangular solid, we find its volume by multiplying its length, width, and height. However, since its length, width, and height are all equal, we can find its volume by *cubing* its side length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =(2\\,\\text{cm})^{3} \\\\  & =(2\\,\\text{cm})\\times (2\\,\\text{cm})\\times (2\\,\\text{cm}) \\\\  & =(2\\times 2\\times 2)\\times (\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}) \\\\  & =8\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189433 #edb/ref 1065 7945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189433 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "15a41542-a66e-5d1f-889a-ca578f48bae4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189433 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating Volume" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440852 #edb/ref 1080 "900\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440852 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440852 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05a416c3-5a8b-5bb4-9e2e-d5d5e3890c12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440853 #edb/ref 1080 "900\\,\\text{ft}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440853 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440853 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06582eb3-c27f-5092-9e9b-b1e567c5c91d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440854 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\text{in}}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440854 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440854 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "