 want to find the area of a forest. What units could we use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440897 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1226ca92-65ae-56a2-b931-338a3cdb6d88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440897 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in kilometers $(\\text{km}).$ When measuring lengths in kilometers, areas are measured in $\\text{km}\\times \\text{km},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a freight car. What units could we use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "230a08c0-5208-5936-927a-cc4ab89b2be1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440898 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in yards $(\\text{yd}).$ When measuring lengths in yards, volumes are measured in $\\text{yd}\\times \\text{yd}\\times \\text{yd},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{yd}}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144164" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a chocolate box. What units could we use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35514c08-5e3f-5179-9038-1219b52d39dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440899 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in centimeters $(\\text{cm}).$ When measuring lengths in centimeters, volumes are measured in $\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{cm}}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1071 "The area of a square with a side length of $9\\,\\text{cm}$ is{{field-1}}\n${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44b69e39-7dc4-5902-a9e6-91ffdc7daa00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440900 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(9\\,\\text{cm})^{2} \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{cm}\\times 9\\,\\text{cm} \\\\  & =(9\\times 9)\\times (\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}) \\\\  & =81\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0c/0c9e721ad5458931b15f8f255f17b9ce02b7973f25e791278da18f4f8997ac68.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the square above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92a736d5-f3b8-5c3c-b7af-b2d6520c2b8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440901 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(7\\,\\text{cm})^{2} \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{cm}\\times 7\\,\\text{cm} \\\\  & =(7\\times 7)\\times (\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}) \\\\  & =49\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to determine the area of the largest airport in the world. What units could we use?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fc21508-9f85-5150-8047-4615f447db2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440902 #edb/ref 1074 "We can measure length in miles $(\\text{mi}).$ When measuring lengths in miles, areas are measured in $\\text{mi}\\times \\text{mi},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/49/49338ad3ab6a7632cbdc6536dc44184458067e0f23c68799f832797a5b88d625.png)\n\nThe area of the square above is{{field-1}}\n${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bbbe35dd-2bbc-5214-98a6-eb9aaf15d8bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440903 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(50\\,\\text{km})^{2} \\\\  & =50\\,\\text{km}\\times 50\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =(50\\times 50)\\times (\\text{km}\\times \\text{km}) \\\\  & =2\\,500\\,{\\text{km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144178" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1071 "If a square has a side length of $30\\,\\text{ft},$ what is its area?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf19de17-406e-5637-9313-1be02592e867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440904 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(30\\,\\text{ft})^{2} \\\\  & =30\\,\\text{ft}\\times 30\\,\\text{ft} \\\\  & =(30\\times 30)\\times (\\text{ft}\\times \\text{ft}) \\\\  & =900\\,{\\text{f